[K
Blue sits between green and violet on the visible spectrum, with wavelengths of roughly 450 to 495 nanometers. It is one
 of the three primary colors of light.[K[14;1HWhere Blue Shows Up[16;1H- The sky looks blue because air scatters short wavelengths more than long ones.
- Deep water appears blue since it absorbs red light and reflects blue.
- Blue pigments like ultramarine were once rarer and costlier than gold.
